    "answer": "To get promoted as a CSM, focus on these steps based on NovaOps's promotion process [documents/handbook/making-a-career.md § Promotion Process]:\n\n1. **Timing**: Promotions happen twice yearly (March and September cycles). Ensure you have at least six months in your current role before applying.\n\n2. **Eligibility**: You need sustained performance at your current level and evidence of operating at the next level [documents/handbook/making-a-career.md § Promotion Process].\n\n3. **Evidence for CSM Promotion**: As a CSM, emphasize these areas in your promotion packet [documents/handbook/titles-for-support.md § Levels]:\n   - Owning complex customer accounts and difficult conversations\n   - Coaching junior teammates\n   - Making cross-functional decisions (e.g., when to involve Jira vs. Salesforce)\n   - Turning customer feedback into actionable product insights\n   - Maintaining customer trust while protecting company boundaries\n\n4. **Packet Contents**: Include current title, proposed title, time in role, effective date, evidence examples, peer input, and any concerns [documents/handbook/making-a-career.md § Promotion Packet Contents].\n\n5. **Calibration**: Your manager will work with People Operations and department leadership to review your packet against standards [documents/handbook/making-a-career.md § Calibration].\n\nTrack your impact through specific outcomes like resolved customer risks, improved processes, or measurable improvements in customer satisfaction rather than just activity metrics [documents/handbook/titles-for-support.md § Promotion Evidence].",
